<!-- WHAT IS GYCT -->
<section>
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">About The Programme</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">What is the Global Youth Climate Training?</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle">Co-developed by the Global Youth Coalition, Oxford Net Zero, and the Smith School of Enterprise and the Environment, GYCT is a free, fully online course that has united thousands of young people (aged 16–35) from around the world to learn from leading climate experts and prepare for roles in international climate policy.</p>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-icon"><i class="fas fa-globe-americas"></i></div>
        <h3>Global Reach, Local Impact</h3>
        <p>65% of participants come from MAPA regions (Most Affected People and Areas). 21% identify as Indigenous youth. Live interpretation in up to 6 languages ensures accessibility for all.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-icon"><i class="fas fa-chalkboard-teacher"></i></div>
        <h3>Expert-Led Sessions</h3>
        <p>Weekly 90-minute sessions: 40 minutes of expert presentation, 40 minutes of interactive Q&A, and 10 minutes of creative climate engagement — art, innovation, and success stories.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-icon"><i class="fas fa-hand-holding-usd"></i></div>
        <h3>COP Bursaries</h3>
        <p>£36,000 invested in youth bursaries to date, enabling exceptional participants from underrepresented groups to attend COP29, COP30, and other international climate forums in person.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-icon"><i class="fas fa-users"></i></div>
        <h3>Community First</h3>
        <p>Structured breakout groups, post-session calls, and city/region hubs foster a genuine peer network across regions and movements — not just a classroom, but a community.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

